From: nancy@genie.slhs.udel.edu
Date:     Thu, 14 Apr 94 0:23:57 GMT
Subject: [#94-4-100] Rule-making games

The game that has a flexible rule-making structure (unlike the
nearly unchangeable set of rules generated in Word Lemma) is
called Nomic, is described in chapter 4 of _Mathemagical Themas_
by Hofstadter, and is being discussed on rec.games.abstract.

The rules in Word Lemma are nearly rather than totally
unchangeable--they are changed by consensus if a contradiction
is discovered.

Nancy Lebovitz

